<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:42:00Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>FIFA rankings: France finish the year on the podium, Morocco break into the top five</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f168d74ae0aaf84ae17ef7f34356fb34f12fd8790ebc8ff3f7a83edfe2e79d5</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T06:16:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261119-fifa-rankings-france-finish-the-year-on-the-podium-morocco-break-into-the-top-five--f103b3dbc602.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261119-fifa-rankings-france-finish-the-year-on-the-podium-morocco-break-into-the-top-five" /><summary type="html">FIFA unveiled its final world ranking of 2026. France remain third in the world, behind Spain and Argentina. Les Bleus have now finished in the top three for the ninth consecutive year. Morocco climb two places to fifth, equalling the best-ever ranking by an African nation, previously achieved by Nigeria in 1994. Brazil drop to seventh, while Senegal remain 18th and Ivory Coast sit 28th.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East crisis poses 'largest threat' to energy security in history, warns IEA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81b914c7d7d51c95d465baa27a847115d360839321204e00526bd95b1ce5d499</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T05:11:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-middle-east-crisis-energy-security-iea--bef2931d058a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-middle-east-crisis-energy-security-iea" /><summary type="html">The International Energy Agency said on Thursday that the Middle East crisis triggered by US and Israeli strikes on Iran in February posed the “largest threat” to energy security in history. It warned that consumers were bearing more of the costs as Iran’s blockade of the Strait of Hormuz disrupted oil shipments.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: Vanuatu calls for UN climate summit reform, warns of backsliding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef93c251206387f4dbb503c73d50c305599b5b8951ae8cda4ac75115deb28718</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T02:00:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding--3de44bf4c890.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding" /><summary type="html">Vanuatu's Environment Minister Ralph Regenvanu has called for changes to the UN climate summit process, accusing a small group of countries of blocking progress and warning that COP31 risks reversing previous commitments.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Xi-Trump-Putin talks live: China, US and Russia leaders to hold landmark three-way meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2aae85d7d469de89ca821da4ca423f5dd195836a04bb78c6cded0590026cd04d</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T01:47:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-xi-trump-putin-talks-live-china-us-russia-leaders-hold-landmark-three-way-meeting--0e21cc420896.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-xi-trump-putin-talks-live-china-us-russia-leaders-hold-landmark-three-way-meeting" /><summary type="html">The leaders of China, the US and Russia are set to hold a first-of-its-kind trilateral meeting on Thursday in the Chinese city of Shenzhen, on the sidelines of an APEC summit. The meeting between Xi Jinping, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin, which Beijing said would involve "safeguarding world peace", has raised fears of a carve-up of the globe into "spheres of influence". Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>24-month matured Comté crowned world’s best cheese</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac20cac342f4ca07129c6263302d301fb63c5d1aedf02426ad431e7766dd3583</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T22:32:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-24-month-matured-comt_-crowned-world-s-best-cheese--ed04116806f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-24-month-matured-comt%C3%A9-crowned-world-s-best-cheese" /><summary type="html">With its nutty flavour and smooth, supple texture, it was aged for two years in a former military fortress in eastern France. Comté, an unpasteurised cow’s milk cheese from the Jura Mountains, has beaten more than five thousand challengers to the top prize at the prestigious annual 'World Cheese Awards'. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington has the story.</summary></entry><entry><title>Inside Limoges City Hall devastated by arson attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6895012f6c94146be9719be8ad2345ff52e53b08d591d18f907fcbcc98715fe7</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T22:23:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261118-inside-limoges-city-hall-devastated-by-arson-attack--1e8e4c4d0333.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261118-inside-limoges-city-hall-devastated-by-arson-attack" /><summary type="html">Work is underway to restore the city hall of Limoges, in central France, which was devastated by an arson attack during riots on October 17. More than €1.7 million has been raised through an online fundraising campaign in the wake of the disaster. Also on the show, the highly anticipated Grand Theft Auto VI has finally been released, with gamers in Oceania among the first to get a taste of the latest instalment in the video game franchise.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Crimea bridge strike: Fact-checking fake videos of damage after Ukraine's attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f34da1165156fc44d4936224ef260b1c3e150890a46b01b9bc41144001aa5f0</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T21:51:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261118-crimea-bridge-strike-fact-checking-fake-videos-of-damage-after-ukraine-s-attack--caeee115f4a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261118-crimea-bridge-strike-fact-checking-fake-videos-of-damage-after-ukraine-s-attack" /><summary type="html">Ukraine struck the Kerch Bridge linking Russia to occupied Crimea, but not all the dramatic footage circulating online is real. Multiple AI-generated videos falsely show the bridge collapsed with extensive damage. Some even used branding resembling a Ukrainian news agency to appear credible. While the bridge was indeed struck and damaged, the viral videos were fabricated using AI, as Vedika Bahl explains.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Bassirou Diomaye Faye excluded from Senegal's ruling party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01e4b57c0904cd3f3730972c395757ed3f007cd104186c8e77e2f4cfa95be3e3</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T21:21:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bassirou-diomaye-faye-excluded-from-senegal-s-ruling-party--66c181d4c833.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bassirou-diomaye-faye-excluded-from-senegal-s-ruling-party" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, the political divorce between Senegal's president and the powerful former prime minister and mentor is official. Also, all of Nigeria's states have shown willingness for a push to create their own police forces. And  in parts of the continent, conflict and a drop in funding have placed huge pressures on children's learning.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Reconstruction begins at Limoges City Hall after devastating fire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5aa948693d9f6e09312dcd76e44fcdcd1e4a1a06f35e025e059371d9809cba13</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T20:31:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/reconstruction-begins-at-limoges-city-hall-after-devastating-fire--1aae5611cc5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/reconstruction-begins-at-limoges-city-hall-after-devastating-fire" /><summary type="html">It's been a month since the nationwide protests that degenerated in violence across France. The dramatic pictures of the historic City Hall in the French city of Limoges set on fire made headlines worldwide. To the relief of many, the reconstruction work on the building has now begun. Since the fire, donations have poured in and already about 80 percent of the necessary funding has been secured. FRANCE 24's Caitlin Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Democrats nominate Jeffries to be first Black House speaker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:995ff2dba7354ffd5399d9c548f4a2624e40ce926f4a5a4f5b2f60da87f30536</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:58:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-democrats-nominate-jeffries-to-be-first-black-house-speaker--1a82a2206b26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-democrats-nominate-jeffries-to-be-first-black-house-speaker" /><summary type="html">Hakeem Jeffries is on the cusp of becoming the first Black speaker of the US House of Representatives after Democrats elected him their leader Wednesday following a sweeping midterm election triumph. Jeffries faced no declared challenger, although opposition from some newly elected progressives had exposed divisions over how Democrats should wield their newfound power. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli army launches ground operation in Hamas-controlled area of Gaza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:831cd5f15db84a9fcb2e54298f3f01083e8f1d43c08257946a481f019e4fabe7</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:55:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-in-hamas-controlled-area-of-gaza--842ad9ad2dc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-in-hamas-controlled-area-of-gaza" /><summary type="html">The Israeli military said it had launched an operation on Wednesday in a Hamas-controlled area of central Gaza, where an AFP journalist saw Israeli tanks position themselves east of the Nuseirat refugee camp. The rare ground operation comes after inconclusive Israeli elections, with the opposition's Gadi Eisenkot trying to form a government without caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who has built his brand on saying he will ensure Israel's security. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Netanyahu's only 2 tickets are racism or starting a war: He stopped acting as a democratic player'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be6d9d64301dfa2f92020e1fd85d6673abc57f9ace4b85c027fe392a6010bdfc</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:45:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261118-netanyahu-s-only-2-tickets-are-racism-or-starting-a-war-he-stopped-acting-as-a-democratic-p--f0085602677a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261118-netanyahu-s-only-2-tickets-are-racism-or-starting-a-war-he-stopped-acting-as-a-democratic-player" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Israeli writer and filmmaker Etgar Keret, author of "The Seven Good Years", joining us from Tel Aviv. Keret argues that Netanyahu is seeking to remain in power, at any cost, including delegitimizing Arab parties and prolonging conflict. “For him, it could be a never-ending war as long as he's in power. He has no incentive to stop it,” he warns. Keret also calls for Israelis to examine how the war in Gaza was conducted, arguing that “the media as a whole ignored the war.”</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Xi welcomes Trump: Does Nvidia scandal upend US-China AI race?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0457927b4e00c66140ec7b949161d6bf3dc0c56fcb514018663ec02f4425224</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:42:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261118-xi-welcomes-trump-does-nvidia-scandal-upend-us-china-ai-race--9efab38c66c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261118-xi-welcomes-trump-does-nvidia-scandal-upend-us-china-ai-race" /><summary type="html">You can strike Jensen Huang from the guest list but good luck steering dinner conversation away from the topic in Shenzhen. The co-founder of the AI computing leader was to accompany the US president to the APEC summit before he was undone by revelations of a dalliance with a Chinese national that happened to coincide with a Singapore client's backdoor skirting of sanctions on its powerful H200 chips.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Hegseth makes surprise trip to Venezuela, renews military cooperation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b4dcef490baa633a7cbd543d10cc9120588fd00dba09b22be0a2cbfd8af242b</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T18:59:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-hegseth-makes-surprise-trip-to-venezuela-renews-military-cooperation--c69718d51c80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-hegseth-makes-surprise-trip-to-venezuela-renews-military-cooperation" /><summary type="html">US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth made an unannounced visit to Caracas on Wednesday, announcing a resumption of military cooperation with Venezuela and vowing to crack down on drug traffickers. The trip marks the highest-level US visit since the ouster of Nicolas Maduro in January, signalling a dramatic shift in relations between the two countries.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine keeps trying to bring down Russia's bridge to Crimea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8224086b01bdf2bbcefb9dcfac307b83262f3af5e4e06f096ce4bd2689697148</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T18:17:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-why-ukraine-keeps-trying-to-bring-down-russia-s-bridge-to-crimea--968a1a06351e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-why-ukraine-keeps-trying-to-bring-down-russia-s-bridge-to-crimea" /><summary type="html">A Ukrainian drone and missile strike on Monday night brought down a stretch of the bridge linking the annexed Crimean Peninsula to Russia, potentially crippling a route long used by Moscow to move men and materiel into Crimea and the southern front. Here’s why Kyiv keeps testing its strength against an infrastructure project that has become synonymous with Russian President Vladimir Putin’s 2014 seizure of the peninsula.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Beijing has supported Moscow but 'China understands that America is way more important than Russia'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa859917ca90c217f7255451e74ec85d8bb43da962479fb897db6ce8ce44f58e</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T17:48:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia--f9f88efc8e97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia" /><summary type="html">Following Xi Jinping's very friendly rare tarmac greeting for Donald Trump, Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Kerry Brown, Professor of Chinese Studies and Director of the Lau China Institute at King's College, London. Brown examines the complex relationship between the world's two largest economies, China's growing diplomatic influence and the competition over artificial intelligence.“China is the diplomatic center of the world,” says Brown, pointing to Beijing's ability to bring together leaders from Russia, the United States, Europe and elsewhere. He argues that China now has “extraordinary convening power" and significant influence over Russia.</summary></entry><entry><title>French ex-PM Philippe pledges to slash spending, hike retirement age as Elysée bid falters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57fdd94cac7866f4d85c26ed0ece0f6fe343f1458b6783297c80f5e86fc88bf6</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T17:16:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261118-french-ex-pm-philippe-pledges-to-slash-spending-hike-retirement-age-as-elys_e-bid-falters--0ac9f55bfbf2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261118-french-ex-pm-philippe-pledges-to-slash-spending-hike-retirement-age-as-elys%C3%A9e-bid-falters" /><summary type="html">Former prime minister Édouard Philippe pledged on Wednesday to slash public spending, scrap France’s statutory 35-hour workweek and raise the retirement age to 65 from the current 62.9 years as he unveiled a slew of measures aimed a staving off economic "catastrophe" for France. An early frontrunner in next year's presidential election, Philippe is now trailing rivals in opinion polls and at risk of missing out on the second-round runoff.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>War in Ukraine: Is France in direct conflict with Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec3602c22cc4178a7d12dc3726f45f7b1604699b8222ea1e915ac0f578cc5240</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:57:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-war-in-ukraine-is-france-in-direct-conflict-with-russia--95e35187e67d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-war-in-ukraine-is-france-in-direct-conflict-with-russia" /><summary type="html">An investigation published by the French public radio channel RFI on November 17 revealed that a confidential mission by the French army known as "Volia" has been used for months to conceal the presence of French personnel in Ukraine. Russia was prompt to accuse France of direct involvement in the conflict. Is this true?</summary></entry><entry><title>Senate leadership challenge exposes divisions among Democrat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22abbc43404a806427b406e4f3e5ef60e2e10f4fefb53169f390109d7c8f6b50</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:39:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-senate-leadership-challenge-exposes-divisions-among-democrat--a320559c5598.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-senate-leadership-challenge-exposes-divisions-among-democrat" /><summary type="html">As Democrats prepare to take control of the Senate, incumbent minority leader Chuck Schumer is facing an insurgent leadership bid from Senator Chris Van Hollen and disputes over party leadership are exposing divisions over what direction to take the Democratic party after their midterms sweep.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia’s new low-cost munitions pose a fresh threat to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbba736019625930389165395177cc28a9dd54354978824910ce58f58a4ce2ea</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:19:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-russia-new-low-cost-munitions-threat-ukraine--81011c427b6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-russia-new-low-cost-munitions-threat-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Dan-T, Filin and Geran-5 might not mean anything to you, but in Ukraine, everyone is talking about these munitions. These new Russian weapons are small, fast and cheap – and a major threat, as they were specially designed to get around Ukrainian anti-aircraft defences and strike deep within the country.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Israel begins new military operation in Gaza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53319309fcf409df87e436a43103778e3c99fdc9bb4b2ef77399e1d62fdf17f7</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:12:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-israel-begins-new-military-operation-in-gaza--3ea99db2529f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-israel-begins-new-military-operation-in-gaza" /><summary type="html">Israeli tanks advanced in an area of the central Gaza Strip on Wednesday, witnesses said, and the Israeli military said its ​forces were targeting ‌Hamas infrastructure outside the "Yellow Line" that sets the boundary of the part of the enclave controlled by Israel  "The IDF launched a precise operation within the Gaza Strip earlier today west of the Yellow Line... to remove a threat posed to IDF troops operating in the Gaza Strip," the military said.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gazans flee shelters as Israeli army launches ground operation beyond Yellow Line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb47477ccc02a2d8d76316750da31b7daa69b197216ed657c6143c7d2dd2a619</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:42:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:03:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-gazans-flee-shelters-as-israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-beyond-yellow-line--9caf8473edb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-gazans-flee-shelters-as-israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-beyond-yellow-line" /><summary type="html">Palestinians fled their tents and shelters in central Gaza on Wednesday after Israel launched a rare ground operation in an area it withdrew ​from under a ‌2025 ceasefire. The Israeli army said it crossed the Yellow Line separating Israeli and Hamas-controlled areas "to remove a threat posed to IDF troops operating in the Gaza Strip".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Why the Houthis may besiege Aden rather than storm it</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58c098e725a32886aee110059bfca3a0a57a564da4a1343a60b2fb00852233a0</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:55:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-yemen-why-the-houthis-may-besiege-aden-rather-than-storm-it--cc45be20d135.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-yemen-why-the-houthis-may-besiege-aden-rather-than-storm-it" /><summary type="html">Bolstered by their recent military successes, Houthi rebels this week advanced close to the southern port city of Aden, the interim capital of the internationally recognised Yemeni government. Amid territorial ambitions, regional rivalries, and divisions within government forces, the potential fall of this stronghold could permanently alter the balance of power in the country.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 US Democrats nominate Hakeem Jeffries to be first Black speaker of the House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69000ac19bacc22f01d7f56c1b32f9a40a4f0489f3593a1f8fd7c63d88a68361</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:45:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-us-democrats-nominate-hakeem-jeffries-to-be-first-black-speaker-of-the-house--380c6ed3ece3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-us-democrats-nominate-hakeem-jeffries-to-be-first-black-speaker-of-the-house" /></entry></feed>
